To pull the **CNAME** DNS records for `sample.com` you’ll hit the *Domain Records* endpoint and filter on record type:

```bash
curl -X GET \
     "https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/sample.com/records?record_type=cname" \
     -H "x-apikey: secret123"
```

### What the response looks like  
A successful reply will contain a JSON payload similar to this:

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "dns_record_01",
      "attributes": { ... }
    },
    {
      "id": "dns_record_02",
      "attributes": { ... }
    }
  ]
}
```

Only the `"id"` field matters here. Extract it from each element inside the `data` array.

---

#### Example “IDs” you would receive (placeholder)

If there were two matching CNAME entries, your extracted list would simply be:

```
["dns_record_01", "dns_record_02"]
```

Replace the placeholder IDs above with whatever appears in your own API response.
